aints, with optimum $(0,3)$ and value 9. What is the solution of the original problem?","options":["$(0,3)$ with value $9$","$(0,-3)$ with value $-9$","$(0,3)$ with value $-9$","$(0,-3)$ with value $9$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c42a10541b4caad0a68e1fc3","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_minimization_to_maximization_577b516a_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A cost-minimization LP is solved as the maximization of the negated cost, and the transformed problem has optimal value $-15$. What is the minimum cost?","options":["$-15$, the transformed value as it stands","$15$, the transformed value with its sign changed","$15$, but only if all cost coefficients are positive","$-15$, since the costs were negated for the run"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0bffa6c2b39bf053c5df65fe","time_limit":35,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_minimization_to_maximization_577b516a_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $\\min\\,2x_1+x_2+7$ subject to $x_1+x_2\\ge12$, $x_1,x_2\\ge0$, a modeller solves $\\max\\,-2x_1-x_2$, dropping the constant, and reports minus its optimal value as the minimum. What is reported, and what is the true minimum?","options":["Reported $19$; true minimum $19$","Reported $-12$; true minimum $-19$","Reported $12$; true minimum $19$","Reported $-19$; true minimum $19$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ab9658a5af5e2fc65181caa6","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_minimization_to_maximization_577b516a_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"The pr